#
# D-0290 + D-0291. Two changes that belong in one build because the first is what makes the
# second safe to add.
#
# D-0290 -- the module's Unix identity. Debug Evolution ran as uid 10001, the SAME uid this
# control plane runs as. NOESAR protects its runtime secrets with owner-only modes (measured
# on this deployment: 1908 files at 0600, 55 directories at 0700, 3 at 0400 across
# NOESAR_EVOLUTION_RUNTIME, NOESAR_EVOLUTION_SHADOWS and config/secrets), and owner-only
# protects nothing between two processes the kernel considers one user -- the module could
# open every module credential in the vault, not only its own. Nothing exploited it; it
# simply was not a boundary. The module now runs as uid/gid 10010 and carries 10001 as a
# supplementary group, which buys exactly one file: its own service token. Verified before
# choosing this over a mask of "the sensitive directories": not one of those 1966 protected
# paths grants read to group 10001 (the only group-readable one is SHADOWS, group 10002 =
# atomd). `server.mjs` writes that token 0640 with the directory at 0710 -- traversable so
# the module can open its token by exact path, unreadable so it cannot list what else is
# there. `chmod` and `chgrp` are what a non-root process CAN do; giving a file away to
# another uid is not, which is why a supplementary group and not a chown.
#
# The identity rather than a list of paths to hide, because a list is a photograph: the next
# secret written somewhere unforeseen would be exposed again in silence. It also matters
# beyond this module -- Debug Evolution is the reference sector module, and every future one
# inherits whatever isolation is established here.
#
# D-0291 -- `/noesar-api/` in the module console proxy. The remote-target screens now live in
# Debug Evolution's own console, and D-0286 decided the module never sees an SSH credential.
# Those two are only compatible if the private key the Owner pastes does not pass through the
# module's process. This prefix is how: the proxy answers it itself and forwards to this
# control plane's own listener with the session cookie intact, so the key travels
# browser -> NOESAR while the module renders the screen and holds nothing. Not a general
# escape hatch -- NOESAR's router authorises those requests exactly as it would on 8088, and
# the proxy's existing session gate has already run before any of it.
#
# Verified before this build: unit 1476/1477 (1 pre-existing skip, 0 failed -- the same count
# D-0286 recorded), ESLint 291 files 0 errors 0 warnings. The uid separation was proven live
# against the running module before this image existed: 0 of 1966 protected files readable,
# direct-path reads refused on all five sensitive targets, the module's own token still read.

FROM noesar-evolution:phase4-debug-evolution-remote-targets

LABEL org.noesar.phase="4-module-uid-separation"
LABEL org.noesar.feature="sector-module-runs-under-its-own-uid-and-remote-target-screens-without-the-module-touching-the-key"
LABEL org.noesar.base-image="noesar-evolution:phase4-debug-evolution-remote-targets"

USER root
COPY --chown=10001:10001 services/reference-control-plane/ /opt/noesar/services/reference-control-plane/
USER 10001:10001
